Based on the provided retrieved code context, there is no implementation of a custom annotation pattern used specifically to inject current authenticated users into controller method parameters. 

However, the context does provide a utility class (`SecurityUtil`) that retrieves the current authenticated user via Spring Security's `SecurityContextHolder`:

```java
package io.spring.graphql;

import io.spring.core.user.User;
import java.util.Optional;
import org.springframework.security.authentication.AnonymousAuthenticationToken;
import org.springframework.security.core.Authentication;
